.TH SKOGAI-MODULE-CHECK 1  "skogai-module-check 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai\-module\-check \- check modules against the spec (docs/module.md), all found ones if none given
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai module check\fR [MODULE]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.br
check modules against the spec (docs/module.md), all found ones if none given
.br

.br
one line per problem: name, error or warn, message. exit 1 on any error;
.br
a missing tool is a warn, it is about this machine, not the module.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR

.TP
[\fIMODULE\fR]...
.br
names, or paths to module dirs
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:"
.TP
\fISKOGAI_SYSTEM_DIR\fR [default: /etc/skogai]
.br
dir of the system layer config
.TP
\fISKOGAI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
.br
dir of the global layer, default ~/.config/skogai
.TP
\fISKOGAI_LOCAL_DIR\fR [default: .skogai]
.br
dir of the local layer; relative is from the git root, or pwd
.TP
\fISKOGAI_MODULE_PATH\fR
.br
colon\-separated dirs of module sources, default the one this module sits in
